# putnami

> polyglot build orchestrator — v0.0.0-golden

## Usage

```
putnami <command[,command...]> [options]
```

## Build Commands

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `putnami build` | Compile or transpile project sources into runnable or distributable outputs |
| `putnami test` | Run the project's tests, emitting test counts and coverage metrics |
| `putnami lint` | Check code for style and correctness findings, emitting per-issue diagnostics |
| `putnami serve` | Run the project's dev server until interrupted |
| `putnami run` | Execute the project once and exit |
| `putnami format` | Rewrite sources into canonical formatting |
| `putnami package` | Assemble distributable artifacts for the project's publish channels |
| `putnami publish` | Push packaged artifacts to registries |
| `putnami deploy` | Converge a cloud environment on the workload's aggregated infra manifest |
| `putnami generate` | Run code generators |

Multi-command: `putnami lint,test,build --impacted`

## Common Options

| Flag | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `--verbose`, `-v` | Show job results and diagnostics |
| `--debug`, `-d` | Stream all events in real-time |
| `--watch`, `-w` | Re-run on file changes |
| `--plan` | Show execution plan without running |
| `--help`, `-h` | Show help |

## Project Selection Options

| Flag | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `--all` | All projects |
| `--impacted` | Projects affected by git changes |
| `--projects` <list> | Comma-separated project names |
| `--tag` <tags> | Filter by tags |
| `--exclude-tag` <tags> | Exclude by tags |
| `--exclude` <names> | Exclude by name |
| `--baseline` <branch> | Custom git baseline for --impacted |
| `--impacted-strict` | Fail when baseline can't be resolved |

## Execution Options

| Flag | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `--where` <placement> | Execution placement: local | remote (local when no runner provider is installed) |
| `--providers` <list> | Credentials to ask the credential provider for: install, publish (comma list) |
| `--credential-fd` <n> | Read the run credential from descriptor <n>; keeps it out of every environment and file; custody level 2 |
| `--no-cache` | Force re-execution (skip cache) |
| `--no-cache-projects` <list> | Force re-execution of these projects only |
| `--cache-trust` <policy> | Remote cache trust: ci | any | none |
| `--continue-on-error` | Don't abort on first failure |
| `--max-parallel` <mode|n> | Parallelism: auto | eco | max | number |
| `--resource` <name=units> | Budget for a named shared resource (repeatable) |
| `--cpu-policy` <policy> | CPU ceiling policy: critical-path | measured |
| `--retry` <n> | Retry transient failures |
| `--retry-failed` | Re-run tasks whose identical failure is cached |
| `--profile` <profile> | Deployment profile: dev | test | production |
| `--dry-run` | Show changes without applying |

## Output Options

| Flag | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `--output` <format> | Output format: text | json | jsonl | cloud-logging |
| `--json` | Shorthand for --output=json |
| `--quiet` | Suppress non-error output |
| `--color` | Force color output |
| `--no-color` | Disable color output |

## Advanced Options

| Flag | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `--trace-profile` <path> | Collect trace events (Chrome trace format) |

## Default Project Selection

With no project target, feature branches run impacted projects vs trunk. On `main` or `master`, Putnami checks the local same-command/params marker first, then an active remote-cache successful-run marker, and falls back to all projects when no usable marker exists.

